id: pm-rl-32a9
title: "pm rl lineage: the generation chain with each hop's promotion evidence and the invalidation frontier"
description: "The chain is the artifact an operator and an agent both need, and reconstructing it from individual item reads costs more context than the answer is worth. One view walks the generation chain and prints, per hop, the base checkpoint, the collection runs, the proxy and held-out scores with their gap, the approval that authorized the hop, and whether anything upstream has since invalidated it. The last column is the one that decides what to do next: a chain that is green to generation four and invalidated from generation two onward means the last two promotions rest on a result that no longer holds, which is exactly the state that is invisible today and expensive to discover by hand."
type: Feature
status: open
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-08-04T20:50:26.547Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-04T20:50:26.547Z"
author: claude
estimated_minutes: 600
acceptance_criteria: The view renders the full chain from seed to head with one row per generation; each row names the promotion evidence and its approval item; invalidated generations are marked with the upstream edit that invalidated them; the view answers from the graph and never recomputes a score; output is available in both a human table and a machine-readable form
